      "id": "https://wan-ifra.org/?p=118467",
      "title": "‘Don’t build on borrowed land’: Times Internet COO on building (and monetising) reader relationships",
      "link": "https://wan-ifra.org/2026/08/dont-build-on-borrowed-land-times-internet-coo-on-the-shift-from-clicks-to-building-and-monetising-reader-relationships/",
      "published": "Tue, 04 Aug 2026 10:03:45 +0000",
      "summary_raw": "<p>As the fundamentals of traffic-based online publishing crumble, publishers need to move fast to redesign their businesses around loyal audiences, says Puneet Gupt: “The ad click era is over. The algorithm era is over. I think we are at the dawn of the relationship era.”</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://wan-ifra.org/2026/08/dont-build-on-borrowed-land-times-internet-coo-on-the-shift-from-clicks-to-building-and-monetising-reader-relationships/\">‘Don&#8217;t build on borrowed land’: Times Internet COO on building (and monetising) reader relationships</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://wan-ifra.org\">WAN-IFRA</a>.</p>",
      "source": "WAN-IFRA"
    },
    {
      "id": "https://wan-ifra.org/?p=118446",
      "title": "Unite for journalism: Ideas to help ignite World News Day",
      "link": "https://wan-ifra.org/2026/08/unite-for-journalism-ideas-to-help-ignite-world-news-day/",
      "published": "Tue, 04 Aug 2026 09:01:54 +0000",
      "summary_raw": "<p>28 September, World News Day, is a moment to highlight and explain your most consequential journalism to the public – and show how and why you do it. Here are some ideas for you to take this year’s campaign to the next level. </p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://wan-ifra.org/2026/08/unite-for-journalism-ideas-to-help-ignite-world-news-day/\">Unite for journalism: Ideas to help ignite World News Day</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://wan-ifra.org\">WAN-IFRA</a>.</p>",
      "source": "WAN-IFRA"
    },
    {
      "id": "https://wan-ifra.org/?p=118506",
      "title": "Harvard Business Review’s Erika Heilman: Growth comes from knowing where to focus",
      "link": "https://wan-ifra.org/2026/08/harvard-business-reviews-erika-heilman-growth-comes-from-knowing-where-to-focus/",
      "published": "Mon, 03 Aug 2026 15:07:09 +0000",
      "summary_raw": "<p>From premium subscriptions to AI, Erika Heilman explains why growth depends on customer insight, disciplined strategy and knowing what not to pursue.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://wan-ifra.org/2026/08/harvard-business-reviews-erika-heilman-growth-comes-from-knowing-where-to-focus/\">Harvard Business Review’s Erika Heilman: Growth comes from knowing where to focus</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://wan-ifra.org\">WAN-IFRA</a>.</p>",
      "source": "WAN-IFRA"
    },
    {
      "id": "https://www.niemanlab.org/?p=252209",
      "title": "U.S. news jobs are more than 3× more likely to be based in Manhattan than they were 25 years ago",
      "link": "https://www.niemanlab.org/2026/08/u-s-news-jobs-are-more-than-3-more-likely-to-be-based-in-manhattan-than-they-were-25-years-ago/",
      "published": "Mon, 03 Aug 2026 18:19:47 +0000",
      "summary_raw": "Ten years ago, I wrote a piece on how the internet was sucking journalistic resources out of the middle of the country and concentrating it on the coasts — primarily New York City. While digital publishing theoretically could have distributed reporters away from high-cost cities, in reality, it reduced the financial returns on local reporting...",
      "source": "Nieman Lab"
    },
